WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.730
This executive order, signed by President
Trump,

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:06.870
starts a new policy on refugees and immigration
in America.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:14.099
TRUMP: "And this is the protection of the
nation from foreign terrorist entry into the

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:15.740
United States..."

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.240
But that's not really what's in this Executive
Order.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.980
So let’s go through it.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.429
First, the executive order banned all immigrants
and visa-holders from seven majority-muslim

00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:28.260
countries from entering the US for at least
90 days.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.320
There is no security benefit.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:36.430
Americans are more likely to be killed by
their own clothes than by an immigrant terrorist.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:40.800
Nobody in the US has been killed in a terrorist
attack by immigrants from these particular

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.320
7 nations.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:47.070
But the US is now treating everybody from
these countries as if they are a suspect.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:54.190
Computational biologist Samira Asgari said
she now can’t come here to work on immunogenomics.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:58.960
Oscar Winner Asghar Farhadi can’t come back
to the US for the Oscars, where he’s nominated

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.470
again.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:05.309
Sudanese Doctor Suha Abushamma hurried back
to the US to begin work at the prestigious

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:09.539
Cleveland Clinic, only to be put back onto
a plane out hours later.

00:01:09.539 --> 00:01:15.049
But in addition to these travel bans, the
executive order also begins a fundamental

00:01:15.049 --> 00:01:17.789
shift in American refugee policy.

00:01:17.789 --> 00:01:23.240
The order halts nearly ALL refugee admissions
for 120 days, and admissions of Syrian refugees

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.790
indefinitely.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:28.719
And it says that in the future, refugees will
only be admitted from countries that have

00:01:28.719 --> 00:01:34.110
sufficient safeguards in place to “ensure
the security and welfare of the United States”

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:39.700
This is the opposite of how the US has defined
refugees in the past: people fleeing persecution

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:44.829
and violence that their own governments cannot
or will not protect them from.

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:49.789
And this comes at a time when the world faces
its biggest refugee crisis since World War II.

00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:53.700
1 in 122 people worldwide are displaced.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.429
And those fleeing the largest humanitarian
emergency of our time -- the Syrian civil

00:01:58.429 --> 00:02:02.560
war -- are the ones singled out by Trump for
harsher restrictions.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:08.170
If you’re worried about US terrorist attacks
like 9/11, San Bernadino, or the Orlando Pulse

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:12.330
shooting – this Order would have prevented
exactly none of them.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.750
But there is an exception for some kinds of
refugees.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:18.010
David Brody, Christian Broadcasting Network:
"As it relates to persecuted Christians, do

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:21.010
you see them as kind of a priority here?"

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:22.010
Trump:"Yes.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.360
They've been horribly treated.”

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.870
The US will allow members of religious minorities
in the individual’s country of nationality

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.080
during the 120 day-ban,

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.410
and prioritize them thereafter.

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:35.891
Trump: "Do you know if you were a Christian
in Syria, it was impossible, very very, at

00:02:35.891 --> 00:02:38.420
least very very tough into the United States.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:44.330
If you were a Muslim you could come in, but
if you were a Christian, it was almost impossible”

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:48.700
In fact, half of refugees in the past few
years were Christian.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:53.350
Refugees from Syria reflected the country’s
religious composition – almost entirely

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:54.350
muslim.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:57.500
But all this aligns with Trump’s anti-Muslim
promises throughout the campaign.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:03.410
Trump: "Donald J. Trump is calling for a total
and complete shutdown of Muslims entering

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.810
the United States."

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:08.150
Trump spoke about taking an “America First”
approach at his inauguration.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:17.000
Trump: "From this day forward it's going to
be only America First.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.010
America First."

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:23.880
This Executive Order shows how much that vision
aligns with the original “America First”

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:24.880
movement.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:28.850
That movement sought American isolationism
too – they were against American intervention

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.360
in World War II.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:36.150
That attitude resulted in the infamous decision
in June 1939 to turn away the St. Louis.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:41.850
That ship had 937 jewish refugees aboard,
fleeing another hostile government: Hitler’s.

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.950
First, they were turned away in Cuba.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.620
"The liner St. Louis, turned back from Cuba"

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.850
Then they approached Florida, but the US Coast
Guard, patrolling the waters, kept them away

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:51.850
too.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:54.590
They eventually disembarked in Belgium, the
Netherlands, and France.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:58.700
"...Jewish unfortunates without a country
permitted to land in Belgium after five weeks

00:03:58.700 --> 00:03:59.700
of suspense afloat..."

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.450
And eventually hundreds died in the holocaust.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:06.520
Since then, the US Government has been the
world’s leader in resettling refugees.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.840
"...They finally reach a haven of safety..."

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:13.030
The State Department website still brags about
it, claiming 3 Million refugees re-settled

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:16.510
around all 50 states since 1975.

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:21.100
The statue of liberty bears these goals too:
a plaque on the pedestal reads:

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.320
"Give me your tired, your poor,

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.940
Your huddled masses yearning to breathe free,

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:28.820
The wretched refuse of your teeming shore.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:31.900
Send these, the homeless, tempest-tost to
me,

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:35.440
I lift my lamp beside the golden door!”

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.160
America hasn’t always lived up to these
lofty goals.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:42.810
But since World War II, we’ve lived in an
era where the diversity of who gets to come

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:46.060
to America has gone up and up.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:51.580
And a Federal Judge stayed deportations of
those stuck in airports amidst the confusion.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.990
And the Trump administration has already started
scaling back.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:57.350
Reince Priebus, White House Chief Of Staff:
"As far as green card holders, moving forward,

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:58.620
it doesn’t affect them.”

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:03.040
The Trump Administration is trying to end
the era when America didn’t care what religion

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.040
you are.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.000
Regardless where you come from.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.000
Legal challenges and protests around the country
continue to try to preserve it.

